{"full":"martin-ueding/geo-activity-playground","name":"geo-activity-playground","description":"Data analysis and visualization based on GPS tracked outdoor activities.","category":"Other","language":"Jupyter Notebook","stars":99,"forks":23,"created":"2022-06-10T16:49:15Z","updated":"2026-09-27T18:30:37Z","license":null,"branch":"main","homepage":"https://martin-ueding.github.io/geo-activity-playground/","topics":[],"demo":null,"color":"#302e55","ink":"#dbd2ff","availability":"available","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-04T05:48:34.708Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-04T05:48:34.708Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-04T05:48:34.708Z","lastDemoCheckedAt":"2026-10-03T08:25:31.008Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-03T21:18:12.850Z","stars":99,"forks":23},{"at":"2026-10-04T05:48:34.708Z","stars":99,"forks":23}],"technologies":[],"overviewAttemptAt":"2026-10-04T05:06:37.567Z","overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["Geo Activity Playground is a software to view recorded outdoor activities and derive various insights from your data collection. All data is kept on your machine, hence it is suitable for people who have an affinity for data analysis and privacy.","It caters to serve a similar purpose as other systems like Strava, Statshunters or VeloViewer, though the focus here is on self-hosting and using local files.","One can use this program with a local collection of activity files (GPX, FIT, TCX, KML, CSV) or via the Strava API. The latter is appealing to people who want to keep their data with Strava primarily. In case that one wants to move, this might provide a noncommittal way of testing out this project."],"features":["Use your GPX, FIT, TCX, KML, or CSV files. Heart rate, cadence, speed and elevation are parsed automatically.","✂️ Activity Trimming","Crop the start or end of a track to remove warm-up noise or accidental recording.","Tag activities and search by name, kind, equipment, date, distance, elevation, or tag — with a map view of results.","📸 Photo Integration"],"